29:  {day:4,loc:'shop',time:'AFTER SCHOOL',speaker:'MR. LEE',title:'The corner shop',objective:'Pick up tea and something small to eat.',text:'Mr. Lee recognizes the photograph from the old neighborhood fair. He remembers a child named Mira who used to trade paper stars for lemon candies. “I don’t know if that is your Mira,” he says. “But I remember the stars.” Outside, the clouds are beginning to lift.',options:[['Ask what the fair was like.','shop_fair'],['Buy a lemon candy and keep the story.','shop_candy'],['Thank him and head out.','shop_leave']]},
30:  {day:4,loc:'center',time:'EARLY EVENING',speaker:'JULES',title:'A room with soft chairs',objective:'Visit the youth centre.',text:'At the youth centre, Jules is setting out mugs for the after-school group. They tell you the room is open to anyone who needs somewhere quiet. No introductions required. On the noticeboard is a flyer for a weekend art table.',options:[['Stay for the art table.','center_art'],['Ask about one-to-one support.','center_support'],['Sit quietly, then go home.','center_quiet']]},
31:  {day:5,loc:'home',time:'MORNING',speaker:'YOU',title:'A name in your own handwriting',objective:'Decide what you want to write in your journal.',text:'You write “Mira” on a fresh page. The name might belong to a friend, a cousin, a story you heard, or a memory not ready to settle. The page does not demand an answer. You notice your shoulders have lowered a little.',fragment:'mira',options:[['Write a letter with no need to send it.','letter_write'],['Write questions instead of answers.','letter_questions'],['Close the journal and make breakfast.','letter_close']]},
32:  {day:5,loc:'school',time:'MIDDAY',speaker:'SAM',title:'Walking beside someone',objective:'Talk with Sam about the week.',text:'Sam asks how the week has been. You tell them it has been more than one thing: tiring, strange, sometimes kind. “I’m glad you let me walk beside you,” they say. You realize support can be ordinary—a seat saved, a message answered, a person who does not rush you.',options:[['Tell Sam what you appreciate.','sam_thanks'],['Ask if they want to hang out this weekend.','sam_weekend'],['Say you need quiet, but not goodbye.','sam_quiet']]},
